            <ArticleTitle>A preliminary study on the analgesic activity of Grangea maderaspatana.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>553-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The methanol extract of the whole plant of Grangea maderaspatana showed a dose-dependent analgesic activity. At doses of 1 and 3 g/kg, the extract significantly (P&lt;0.001) inhibited acetic acid-induced writhing in mice by 50 and 80%, respectively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
